{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015v8y4viT2ES6NbWCcj3UVk","type":"tool_result","content":" * @property {string} url   WebSocket URL of the engine sidecar.\n * @property {string} token Per-launch credential the sidecar expects.\n */\n\n/**\n * Ask the host where the engine sidecar is listening (US-070).\n *\n * Electron asked the deleted `src/main/engine-process.js`; this one\n * asks `src-tauri/src/engine.rs`, which supervises the same sidecar\n * (ADR-012) and answers the same `{ url, token }`. The host waits out\n * a restart before replying, so a slow answer here means the engine is\n * on its way back rather than that the call was lost.\n *\n * The port changes when the sidecar restarts, so this is a question to\n * ask on every connect rather than a value to cache. `null` means the\n * host has no engine to offer -- `ipc-engine.js` retries.\n *\n * @returns {Promise<EngineEndpoint|null>}\n */\nexport async function getEngineEndpoint () {\n  return invoke('get_engine_endpoint')\n}\n\nexport async function onLog (listener, options) {\n  notImplemented('ipc-os', 'onLog')\n}\n\nexport async function onError (listener, options) {\n  notImplemented('ipc-os', 'onError')\n}\n\nsrc/renderer/lib/platform/AGENTS.md:255:  one argument (`onDispatch`, and `onLog`/`onError` when they land)\ndocs/platform-shim.md:103:| `dialog.showOpenDialog`, `showSaveDialog` | US-058 | one host command each, over the dialog plugin's **Rust** API; the options translation is `src-tauri/src/dialog.rs` |\ndocs/platform-shim.md:149:top of `src-tauri/src/dialog.rs`:\ndocs/platform-shim.md:649:| `onLog(listener, opts)` | `log` | `main.js:340` |\ndocs/platform-shim.md:650:| `onError(listener, opts)` | `error` | `main.js:341` |\ndocs/platform-shim.md:692:| `onError(listener, opts)` | `castError` | a message for `state.errors` |\ndocs/platform-shim.md:706:poll that hangs cannot stall the UI thread. `onError` exists because\ncast.rs\nclipboard.rs\ndialog.rs\ndock.rs\nengine.rs\nexternal_player.rs\nfs.rs\nmain.rs\nmenu.rs\npaths.rs\npower.rs\nready.rs\nshell.rs\nshortcuts.rs\nstartup.rs\ntray.rs\nupdater.rs\nwatcher.rs\nwindow.rs\n21:    \"test\": \"npm run lint && depcheck --ignores=standard,eslint,@babel/eslint-parser,madr,buffer,nightralph --ignore-dirs=build,build-vite,build-tauri,build-sidecar,dist && npm run test-unit\",\n22:    \"test-unit\": \"npm run build && tape test/unit/*.js\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10e52fa7-0731-4e0f-9efd-cb735ba1e975","uuid":"48175577-0c0b-48d1-aa72-4b94f10f7186","timestamp":"2026-10-13T05:30:22.514Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" * @property {string} url   WebSocket URL of the engine sidecar.\n * @property {string} token Per-launch credential the sidecar expects.\n */\n\n/**\n * Ask the host where the engine sidecar is listening (US-070).\n *\n * Electron asked the deleted `src/main/engine-process.js`; this one\n * asks `src-tauri/src/engine.rs`, which supervises the same sidecar\n * (ADR-012) and answers the same `{ url, token }`. The host waits out\n * a restart before replying, so a slow answer here means the engine is\n * on its way back rather than that the call was lost.\n *\n * The port changes when the sidecar restarts, so this is a question to\n * ask on every connect rather than a value to cache. `null` means the\n * host has no engine to offer -- `ipc-engine.js` retries.\n *\n * @returns {Promise<EngineEndpoint|null>}\n */\nexport async function getEngineEndpoint () {\n  return invoke('get_engine_endpoint')\n}\n\nexport async function onLog (listener, options) {\n  notImplemented('ipc-os', 'onLog')\n}\n\nexport async function onError (listener, options) {\n  notImplemented('ipc-os', 'onError')\n}\n\nsrc/renderer/lib/platform/AGENTS.md:255:  one argument (`onDispatch`, and `onLog`/`onError` when they land)\ndocs/platform-shim.md:103:| `dialog.showOpenDialog`, `showSaveDialog` | US-058 | one host command each, over the dialog plugin's **Rust** 